  "$comment": "Hero looks (docs/hero-looks.md §3.1, §6, §7): the one catalog of coats, nameplate frames and titles a hero may choose. Mirrors LookCatalog in packages/shared/src/types/look.ts. Starter looks are free for every hero and never stored; every other look is held through a receipt on her own look (LookUnlock). Earned ones are given by a receipt (#669, packages/shared/src/look-unlocks.ts): a found look by a chapter's findLook effect (content/README.md, Look finds), a milestone (tier, class rank, finished campaign, camp friend, first friend, grand camp) when it lands and on read. Coats (#666) are colours for one species' coloured region (her coat, mane, scales, feathers or fur; the kid sees the shelf as Color): about six starters per species, natural for it, each checked against every backdrop and its siblings under colour-blind vision by packages/client/src/world/coat-palette.test.ts. A special coat (two-tone, shimmer; #669) keeps a color, its base, and adds an effect; special coats are earned only. A frame's painting is UI art (#665) at assets/<art>; until assets/manifest.json -> nameplateFrames.ids lists it as delivered, the plain plate (today's look) is drawn instead and nothing is requested. Titles are kept short: the longest one is what the nameplate collision tests are run with.",
